    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19142" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fuscus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname;</i>
			e. g., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Aristius
			Fuscus, <i>an intimate friend of Horace;</i> v.
			Aristius.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Fuscus, <i>a soldier</i>, <i>courtier</i>, <i>and sensualist of the time of
				Domitian</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 2, 86</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 6,
			76</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 4, 112</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fuscī-nus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a Fuscus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">explicationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Suas. 4 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
